5) Terraform snippet (IAM role + instance profile + optional alarm)

Minimal example to create IAM role & policy and instance profile:

# provider must be configured externally
resource "aws_iam_role" "ec2_process_monitor" {
  name = "ec2_process_monitor_role"
  assume_role_policy = data.aws_iam_policy_document.ec2_assume_role.json
}

data "aws_iam_policy_document" "ec2_assume_role" {
  statement {
    effect = "Allow"
    principals {
      type = "Service"
      identifiers = ["ec2.amazonaws.com"]
    }
    actions = ["sts:AssumeRole"]
  }
}

resource "aws_iam_policy" "process_monitor_policy" {
  name        = "ProcessMonitorPolicy"
  description = "Allow put metric data"
  policy      = file("${path.module}/process_monitor_policy.json") # write policy json (from earlier) here
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "attach_policy" {
  role       = aws_iam_role.ec2_process_monitor.name
  policy_arn = aws_iam_policy.process_monitor_policy.arn
}

resource "aws_iam_instance_profile" "ec2_profile" {
  name = "ec2_process_monitor_instance_profile"
  role = aws_iam_role.ec2_process_monitor.name
}


Terraform for CloudWatch alarm (one example for a process):

resource "aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm" "process_down" {
  alarm_name          = "ProcessDown-my_app_1"
  alarm_description   = "Alarm if my_app_1 is down for 4 minutes"
  comparison_operator = "LessThanOrEqualToThreshold"
  evaluation_periods  = 2
  metric_name         = "ProcessStatus"
  namespace           = "Custom/ProcessMonitor"
  period              = 120
  statistic           = "Average"
  threshold           = 0.5
  dimensions = {
    ProcessName = "my_app_1"
  }
  alarm_actions = [aws_sns_topic.notify.arn] # define SNS topic elsewhere
}

6) Grafana: visualize & alert
Option A — Recommended approach

Use CloudWatch Alarms for reliable alerting (they’re built for it). Then in Grafana you:

Add CloudWatch as a datasource (AWS credentials or assume role).

Visualize the Custom/ProcessMonitor metric with dimension ProcessName.

Use the CloudWatch alarm for notifications / paging. Grafana can also read alarms as annotations.

Option B — Grafana alerting (query CloudWatch metric directly)

If you want Grafana-native alerts, create metric queries to CloudWatch: query the ProcessStatus metric for each process and create an alert rule that fires if the metric averages below 0.5 over the last 4 minutes.

Steps in Grafana (v8+ alerting):

Add CloudWatch datasource: Configure credentials/assume-role and region.

Create a new dashboard -> panel -> Query:

Namespace: Custom/ProcessMonitor

Metric name: ProcessStatus

Dimension: ProcessName = my_app_1

Period: 2m

In the panel, create an alert rule:

Condition: WHEN avg() OF query(A, 2m, now) IS BELOW 0.5

For: 4m (or set evaluation to require 2 evaluation cycles)

Configure notifications (Slack, email, webhook via Grafana contact point).

Note: Grafana alert evaluation cadence depends on Grafana server settings. CloudWatch Alarms are generally more reliable for on-call notifications.

